Package: phytogrowR
Type: Package
Title: Modern Growth Analysis for Plant Biomass and Leaf Area Data
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Joao Everthon da Silva",
           family = "Ribeiro",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "everthonribeiro10@gmail.com")
  )
Description: Tools for classical and functional plant growth analysis from
    sequential and destructive harvests, repeated measurements, and time series
    of biomass and leaf area. Estimates relative growth rate, absolute growth
    rate, unit leaf rate (also known as net assimilation rate), leaf area ratio,
    specific leaf area, leaf weight fraction, crop growth rate, biomass
    partitioning, root-shoot ratios, and root-shoot allometric coefficients.
    Interval formulae and their assumptions follow Radford (1967)
    <doi:10.2135/cropsci1967.0011183X000700030001x>, the computational and
    design recommendations of Poorter and Garnier (1996)
    <doi:10.1093/jxb/47.9.1343>, and the classical implementation of Hunt,
    Causton, Shipley and Askew (2002) <doi:10.1093/aob/mcf214>. Functional
    approaches include curve fitting, numerical derivatives, bootstrap
    confidence intervals, formal tests of curve coincidence between treatments
    based on nested models, publication-ready graphics, and an optional 'shiny'
    interface.
